# Default DRF Settings

In Django REST Framework (DRF), Default DRF Settings ka matlab hota hai:

> Baar baar har view me same configuration likhne ke bajaye ek central place par DRF ki global settings define kar dena.

Ye settings usually `settings.py` me hoti hain.

---

## Basic Structure

```python
# settings.py

REST_FRAMEWORK = {

}
```

Is dictionary ke andar DRF ki sari default configurations aati hain.

---

# Most Important Default DRF Settings

---

## 1. Default Authentication Classes

Agar har API me authentication chahiye to baar baar:

```python
authentication_classes = [TokenAuthentication]
```

likhne ki zarurat nahi.

Global setting:

```python
REST_FRAMEWORK = {
    'DEFAULT_AUTHENTICATION_CLASSES': [
        'rest_framework.authentication.TokenAuthentication',
    ]
}
```

Ab sab APIs automatically token auth use karengi.

---

## 2. Default Permission Classes

Har view me:

```python
permission_classes = [IsAuthenticated]
```

likhne ke bajaye:

```python
REST_FRAMEWORK = {
    'DEFAULT_PERMISSION_CLASSES': [
        'rest_framework.permissions.IsAuthenticated',
    ]
}
```

Ab sari APIs login require karengi by default.

---

## 3. Default Renderer Classes

API browser show karna hai ya sirf JSON?

```python
REST_FRAMEWORK = {
    'DEFAULT_RENDERER_CLASSES': [
        'rest_framework.renderers.JSONRenderer',
    ]
}
```

Isse browsable API band ho jayegi.

---

## 4. Default Parser Classes

Request body ka data kaise parse hoga.

```python
REST_FRAMEWORK = {
    'DEFAULT_PARSER_CLASSES': [
        'rest_framework.parsers.JSONParser',
    ]
}
```

---

## 5. Pagination

Automatic pagination.

```python
REST_FRAMEWORK = {
    'DEFAULT_PAGINATION_CLASS':
        'rest_framework.pagination.PageNumberPagination',

    'PAGE_SIZE': 5
}
```

Ab response:

```json
{
   "count":20,
   "next":"...",
   "previous":"...",
   "results":[]
}
```

---

## 6. Throttling (Rate Limiting)

Ek user kitni requests bhej sakta hai.

```python
REST_FRAMEWORK = {
    'DEFAULT_THROTTLE_CLASSES': [
        'rest_framework.throttling.UserRateThrottle',
    ],

    'DEFAULT_THROTTLE_RATES': {
        'user': '10/minute',
    }
}
```

---

## 7. Default Filter Backends

```python
REST_FRAMEWORK = {
    'DEFAULT_FILTER_BACKENDS': [
        'django_filters.rest_framework.DjangoFilterBackend'
    ]
}
```

---

# Real Production Example

```python
REST_FRAMEWORK = {

    'DEFAULT_AUTHENTICATION_CLASSES': [
        'rest_framework.authentication.TokenAuthentication',
    ],

    'DEFAULT_PERMISSION_CLASSES': [
        'rest_framework.permissions.IsAuthenticated',
    ],

    'DEFAULT_RENDERER_CLASSES': [
        'rest_framework.renderers.JSONRenderer',
    ],

    'DEFAULT_PAGINATION_CLASS':
        'rest_framework.pagination.PageNumberPagination',

    'PAGE_SIZE': 10,
}
```

---

# Flow Samjho

## Without Default Settings

```python
class ProductView(APIView):

    authentication_classes=[TokenAuthentication]
    permission_classes=[IsAuthenticated]
```

Har file me repeat karna padta hai.

---

## With Default Settings

```python
class ProductView(APIView):
    pass
```

Kyuki DRF automatically `settings.py` se settings uthata hai.

---

# Override Bhi Kar Sakte Ho

Global setting:

```python
DEFAULT_PERMISSION_CLASSES:
IsAuthenticated
```

Lekin kisi ek view ko public banana ho:

```python
from rest_framework.permissions import AllowAny

class PublicView(APIView):
    permission_classes=[AllowAny]
```

Ye global setting ko override kar dega.

---

# Important Interview Line

> DRF default settings are global configurations defined in `REST_FRAMEWORK` inside `settings.py` to avoid repetitive configuration across views.

---

# Most Asked DRF Default Settings

| Setting | Purpose |
|---|---|
| DEFAULT_AUTHENTICATION_CLASSES | Authentication define karta |
| DEFAULT_PERMISSION_CLASSES | Permissions define karta |
| DEFAULT_RENDERER_CLASSES | Response format define karta |
| DEFAULT_PARSER_CLASSES | Request parsing |
| DEFAULT_PAGINATION_CLASS | Pagination |
| DEFAULT_THROTTLE_CLASSES | Rate limiting |
| DEFAULT_FILTER_BACKENDS | Filtering |
